From cf18f68100b7b2c94874f9c7a99016acaf684b60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aclater <105859+aclater@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:35:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] avformat: add DSF muxer

Writes DSD Stream File from the DSD codecs (dsd_lsbf, dsd_msbf and their
planar variants), 1 to 6 channels. The audio is written least significant
bit first in blocks of 4096 bytes per channel, the last block padded with
zeros, as most DSF files are; most significant bit first input is
bit-reversed. The file size, sample count and data size are written by the
trailer. Global metadata and chapters go into an ID3v2 tag after the data.

The channel type follows the layouts the DSF demuxer reads, so that files
round-trip.

Signed-off-by: aclater <105859+aclater@users.noreply.github.com>
